              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भूरो (bhūro) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from bhrūra, \"brown\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants. CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry (CDIAL 9690); the match is through Hindi bhūrā and Gujarati bhūrũ. CDIAL sets it beside Indo-European bhrūno-, behind English brown."
